From aa8e3090dc21a756270a1dbed226ca7a7f8f39e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:37:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 110/119] fix: the previews were being lit in absolute units
 and shown as if they were not

A ccam ticked in the level made the material editor preview, every asset thumbnail,
the Character Tool, the Schematyc preview and the 2D viewports scene-referred too:
CRendererResources::IsSceneReferred() is a device-global question with no pipeline in
it, and exactly one of the 6-10 pipelines a routine editor session runs owns a tone
map. The others received the pre-exposure, the 1/PI convention and the fp16 reformats
with nothing to undo any of it - a white square at an interior camera, black at
daylight, and the thumbnail then written to disk and cached.

Scene-referred becomes a property of a pipeline that owns a display transform. A new
virtual CGraphicsPipeline::IsSceneReferredCapable(), true only on
CStandardGraphicsPipeline, is evaluated once per render view in
LatchSceneReferredExposure() and published as a render-thread gate that
IsSceneReferred() ANDs in - so the exposure, the formats, the working space, the ODT,
the inert LDR stage, the thresholds and the export tap all follow from one chokepoint
instead of three, and cannot drift apart later. The gate defaults to OPEN, so it can
only ever take work away from a render, never add it.

The terrain minimap rides the same gate: e_ScreenShot modes 3-6 render through the
level's own Standard pipeline and must not carry the camera's exposure, sensor clip,
white balance, CDL and ODT. A minimap is data. e_ScreenShot 1 (high-res) is
deliberately not in the list - a high-res screenshot IS the picture. The cvar is read
on the render thread and so the gate is coarse by a frame or two around the bake,
which is harmless because the bake is modal.

Exposure is per pipeline; the CONVENTION stays global. E3DPARAM_SCENE_REFERRED changes
the sun's own colour and there is one sun for every view, so withholding the 1/PI from
a preview would leave it PI times too bright. m_fSceneReferredBRDFFactor and the skybox
emittance unit in S3DEngineCommon::UpdateSkyInfo (main thread, one m_SkyInfo for every
view) therefore ask the new un-gated IsSceneReferredRequested*() instead.
Probe bakes are byte-identical: SHDF_CUBEMAPGEN keeps its own exposure force.

Instrumentation: one CryLogAlways per gate DECISION naming the pipeline and the reason,
and a first r_HDRDebug 1 line "pipeline: <name> scene-referred: yes/no".

Notes: scene-notes/decisions/s8-preview-gate.md, research/s8-editor-pipelines.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus <noreply@anthropic.com>
